-Failure protocol:
-
-- If a verification command fails or produces errors, stop the current automatic progression.
-- Explain the error in eva-results/iteration-N-process-summary.md.
-- Classify the failure as one of:
-  - generated process syntax error;
-  - generated thread syntax error;
-  - missing process/thread containment;
-  - invalid port direction/type/status;
-  - invalid DataPort/EventDataPort selection;
-  - missing or invalid connection endpoint;
-  - invalid scheduling/domain/binding attribute;
-  - HAMR subset violation;
-  - namespace/type/field-access error;
-  - GUMBO attachment-location error;
-  - imported-library/profile/shim issue;
-  - time-unit compatibility issue;
-  - generated-code marker-region issue;
-  - application-logic failure;
-  - verifier/toolchain/environment blocker.
-- Propose a repair plan.
-- If this is an interactive run, wait for user approval before continuing when the repair would modify existing application logic, generated code, or held-out examples.
-- For this experiment, when repairing generated process definitions, keep application logic unchanged unless explicitly approved.
-- Prefer repairing only the generated SysML v2 process/thread/port/connection fragment or GUMBO attachment location.
